<article class="env-remark" id="0FJY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FJY">Remark <span data-tag="0FJY">36.39.2</span>.</a> The construction of Lemma <a href="/tag/0FJX" data-tag="0FJX">36.39.1</a> is compatible with pullbacks. More precisely, given a morphism $f : X \to Y$ of schemes and a perfect object $K$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ Y)$ of tor-amplitude in $[-1, 0]$ then $Lf^*K$ is a perfect object $K$ of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ of tor-amplitude in $[-1, 0]$ and we have a canonical identification </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f^*\det (K) \longrightarrow \det (Lf^*K)  \]
</div>
  <p> Moreover, if $K$ has rank $0$, then $\delta (K)$ pulls back to $\delta (Lf^*K)$ via this map. This is clear from the affine local construction of the determinant. </p>
</article>